fact WorkItem(id: "WI-241", description: some(value: "Loader fails to wrap apply-arg values as ExprOccurrence handles when the underlying parse term has no source span, breaking the occurrence-native typer for nested calls. Symptom: cmd_add_test (anthill-todo) crashes at runtime with 'var_ref(__req_main) unbound in requirement position' because cmd_add's call to do_add — and do_add's args (including the inner collect_all_bindings calls) — go through check_apply with current_occ=None, classify(kb, None, ...) silently no-ops, req_insertion::run skips the call, and the callee runs with empty frame.requirements. Diagnostic walk: (1) debug at the ConcreteApplyWithin classify site shows `occ=None` for the cmd_add→collect_all_bindings classifications while collect_all_bindings_acc→itself classifications (different body) have `occ=Some(N)`. (2) debug inside check_apply's arg-descent loop shows EVERY arg of `do_add(store, description, collect_all_bindings(...), collect_all_bindings(...))` has `arg_occ=None` (split_handle on the ApplyArg.value returns None). (3) debug inside load_apply_or_constructor's convert_expr_child shows `maybe_create_occurrence` returns None because `self.parsed.terms.spans.get(&parse_id)` returns None — many parse terms (simple Idents, nested Fn nodes) lack a span entry, so the loader can't allocate an OccurrenceId, and convert_expr_child falls back to returning the raw term without the Handle wrapper. Per docs/design/expr-occurrences.md §'The Expr IR is occurrence-structured' EVERY child slot MUST be an ExprOccurrence — the current state where ~half the slots are bare terms violates the invariant the typer's occurrence-native rewrite (a5bba1b) was built against. Fix is in the LOADER, not the typer: `convert_expr_child` (anthill-core/src/kb/load.rs:3312) must always produce an OccurrenceId, falling back to a synthesized span (inherited from the enclosing parse term, or a 'no-source-span' sentinel) when the parser didn't stamp one. Alternative: fix the parser/converter to stamp spans on every produced term so maybe_create_occurrence always finds one. Both paths satisfy the invariant; the loader-fallback path is more defensive. Acceptance: every ExprOccurrence-typed child slot in a loaded KB is a Handle (no bare Term::Fn / Term::Ref at ExprOccurrence positions); cmd_add_test + wi203_store_test runtime no longer hits 'var_ref(__req_main) unbound'. Independent of WI-240 (which fixes the typer's Ordered.lt stderr line) — both must land for the bundle tests to pass."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-237"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-15T11:06:48Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-241", author: "claude", content: "Delivered via parser/converter fix, not the loader-fallback alternative described in the original WI. Rather than synthesizing fallback spans at load time, made the every-term-has-a-span invariant STRUCTURAL in the parse IR itself: SimpleTermStore.alloc(term, span) is the only constructor — span is required. Implementation in commit 6db362f: (a) `parse/ir.rs` SimpleTermStore now holds `Vec<ParseTermEntry { term, span }>` instead of `Vec<Term>` + sparse `HashMap<TermId, Span>`. (b) `parse/convert.rs` ~25 alloc sites updated to thread span (mostly via `self.span(node)` at function entry); `alloc_fn_term` gains a span param; new `alloc_bottom(span)` helper; `convert_term_with_span` / `convert_pattern_with_span` removed (their span-stamping moved into alloc). (c) `parse/pratt.rs` synthesized op-nodes use `op_span(terms, first, last)` = Span::merge of operand spans (prefix-op nodes drop operator-token offset, accepted trade-off); outer_span plumbing dropped from desugar. (d) `kb/load.rs` `maybe_create_occurrence{,_ex}` renamed `create_occurrence{,_ex}` returning `OccurrenceId` (not Option); `convert_expr_term` returns `(TermId, OccurrenceId)`; `convert_expr_child` drops None-fallback branch. /simplify pass: restored 4 WI-224 load-bearing comments dropped during refactor, replaced 3 inline Term::Bottom allocs with alloc_bottom, migrated convert_set_literal to alloc_fn_term, trimmed diff-narrating doc-comments. Followup commit eb4482b: cpp-gen `field_name_from_apply_arg` unwraps the Handle that now wraps EVERY Expr child (was: only some); `parse_test::parse_records_term_spans` updated for the removed HashMap field. cmd_add_test (6 tests, was 5 failing) and wi203_store_test (1 test, was failing) all pass. All anthill-core integration tests + cpp-gen 100/100 + workspace doc-tests green. The deeper structural concern — that OccurrenceId is squeezed into Term::Const(Literal::Handle) instead of being a first-class slot type — is filed as WI-242 (Take OccurrenceId out of Term; add Value::Expr; generators read via existing TermView/ViewItem polymorphic binding). WI-242 supersedes the small Handle-unwrap shims this WI added (cpp-gen and the analogous sites in typer/eval).", at: "2026-05-15T11:06:48Z")
